 "response": "Gitrel's budget is now **$2,805K**.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. **Source.** Only Finance Office budget entries count. Messages from Marketing, Sales, Legal, Engineering, Operations, the PMO, Facilities and vendors were ignored. Non-budget Finance notes were also ignored, such as cost center codes, reminders, audits and room moves.\n\n2. **Starting point.** The budget was set to $2,220K in #0001, and there was no later \"set\" entry.\n\n3. **Withdrawal chains.** I resolved each chain from its last link backwards. An unwithdrawn withdrawal takes effect; a withdrawn one does not, which revives whatever it targeted. Examples:\n   - #0002 (+$117K) is cancelled. The chain #0537 \u2192 #0092 \u2192 #0071 \u2192 #0033 \u2192 #0005 \u2192 #0002 ends with #0005 standing.\n   - #0008 (+$288K) is reinstated. #1348 cancels #0194, so #0170 stands and voids #0009.\n   - #0006 (\u2212$556K) stays cancelled. #0185 voids #0029, so #0019 stands.\n   - #0026 (+$112K) is cancelled by #0770, which no one withdrew.\n\n   This left about 93 updates void, among them #0003, #0016, #0036, #0042, #0076, #0147, #0206 and #0281's neighbours #0285 and #0294.\n\n4. **Sum.** I applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order. Some checkpoints in the running total:\n\n| After record | Running total |\n|---|---|\n| #0034 | $2,993K |\n| #0290 | $431K |\n| #0741 | $1,342K |\n| #1314 | $3,525K |\n| #1426 | $4,335K (peak) |\n| #1600 | $2,805K |\n\nANSWER: $2805K",
